From 12d5fa3c51bc2d4af63b0c72726d5b10b703bc47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Atlas agent <agent@atlas.local>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:00:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] used_resources: uses_sorted, a uses question by binary search
 (for a program's check of many objects)

Submission::uses_sorted and CommandBuffer::uses_sorted answer as uses for identities sorted ascending,
each identity the commands name looked up by binary search, not by a scan of all of them (Among). Reims's
submission check asks on every submission, on the scheduler's thread inside its pass, whether the
submission uses any detached object; with hundreds detached, the scan per used resource (names_any) and
Reims's list made for each check took a fifth of that thread's CPU in production (2026-11-14 profile:
run_checks 18-24%, names_any 5%). The submission-check lanes assert the sorted answer is the scan's on
every submission they check; a unit test checks Among against a scan, and that an unsorted list said
sorted is caught in a debug build.
